# ===== THE SEVEN DRAWBRIDGES =============================================================================================
# Each causeway's boardwalk across the mere (in a frame along it: local x 0 at the mere's shore, 64 m out, +x towards
# the town); at its end the windlass (a drum on a post); the gap's lowered deck (hidden till lowered), the raised leaf
# standing at the town's shore (two radio tower walls on two posts), the bridge's zone on the town's side (hidden till lowered)
# (1: the Reed Bridge, from Reedcut)
