# ===== Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest (35 steps, 9 chapters) =============================================
info title=The Great Fen
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A vast forested wetland of reeds, channels and meres, seven stilt villages round its rim and in the middle the lost town of Sevenbridge, cut off since its seven drawbridges were raised. Each bridge belongs to a village, and each village wants something done first.
island on.arrive=message||Reeds and willows and water to the horizon, stilt villages on the firmer ground - and in the middle of a great mere, a town on an island with seven drawbridges standing up like hands raised against you.

story bridgepin|Bridge pin|quest:Varuna_CraneKey|An iron pin as long as your forearm: the Eel Bridge's windlass won't turn without it.
story fenmint|Fen-mint|Placeable_Utopia_Herb_6|A bunch of fen-mint from the hermit's isle, sharp enough to make your eyes water.
story townseal|Sevenbridge's seal|quest:Tangaroa_Token|The town seal, dropped from the town bell's rope when it rings for seven bridges.

note wardenmap The fen-warden's map | THE GREAT FEN - WARDEN'S MAP\n\nSevenbridge raised its seven bridges in the fever year. Each windlass is held by a village:\nREEDCUT (north) - the Reed Bridge. EELMARSH (north-east) - the Eel Bridge. MOTHWICK (east) - the Wisp Bridge. TURFHOLM (south-east) - the Turf Bridge. HERONSBY (south) - the Heron Bridge. WILLOWBEND (west) - the Mill Bridge. STILLWATER (north-west) - the Still Bridge.\nEach village will lower its bridge for whoever helps it. When all seven are down, ring the town bell: the hall's vault opens.\nNet launcher in my chest - Reedcut's geese are loose again.
note wardenchest Warden's chest | The fen-warden's chest: a net launcher, a bundle of net canisters, a bag of smoked herring.
loot wardenchest NetGun*1;NetCanister*8;Cooked_Herring*2
prop wardenchest loot.refill=0
note reedelder Reedcut's elder | REEDCUT - TO WHOEVER COMES\n\nOur geese are loose in the reeds, three of them, and we're too old to run. Net them and they'll go home. Then turn our windlass - the Reed Bridge is yours.
note eelelder Eelmarsh's elder | EELMARSH\n\nThe Eel Bridge's pin is in the old trap at the bottom of our pool - it fell in the year the bridges went up. Seven metres. There's air under the sunk punt. Fetch it and put it in the windlass at our causeway's end, out on the mere.
note wisprhyme The wisp rhyme | (painted on Mothwick's board)\n\nCall the wisp the old way:\nfirst the REED horn, low and long,\nthen the HERON's, sharp as a beak,\nlast the WILLOW's, soft as leaves.\nIt comes to the islet. Stand in its light, and our bridge comes down.
note turfelder Turfholm's elder | TURFHOLM\n\nThe bog boars are in the cutting again - four of them. We can't cut turf, we can't sleep. Drive them off and we'll let down the Turf Bridge.
note healernote The healer's request | HERONSBY - THE HEALER\n\nI need fen-mint for my remedies, and it only grows on the hermit's isle, out in the pools west of here. Bring me a bunch and the Heron Bridge comes down - I hold its windlass.
note locknote The lock-keeper's note | WILLOWBEND LOCK\n\nThe mill isle is only reached through the lock. Pull the lever: the near gate opens for a minute, then shuts. Swim or punt through quick.\nThe miller holds the Mill Bridge's windlass on the isle.
note stillnote The last villager's warning | STILLWATER\n\nThe Bog Beast came out of the mere the night the bridges went up and sleeps on our causeway. Everyone else has gone to Heronsby. The Still Bridge's windlass is at the causeway's end - past it.
note charter The Sevenbridge charter | SEVENBRIDGE - CHARTER OF THE TOWN\n\nThe town stands on seven bridges and is ruled by none.\nIn time of danger the bridges are raised; when all seven are down again, the town bell is rung, and the town's hoard is opened for whoever brought the town back to the fen.
note hoard Sevenbridge's hoard | The town's hoard: seven villages' worth of savings, the plans for the town's great planting beds and for the recycler that made rope from reeds, eel-skin leather, and bars of titanium.
loot hoard TradeToken*25;Blueprint_Cropplot_Large_Tier3*1;Blueprint_Recycler*1;Leather*6;TitaniumIngot*3;Rope*6
prop hoard loot.refill=0
prop hoard if.open=has|story:townseal|1
prop hoard else.open=message||The town's hoard, locked. The charter says how it opens.
note eeltrap The old eel trap | The old eel trap at the bottom of the pool: an eel's skeleton - and the Eel Bridge's iron pin.
loot eeltrap story:bridgepin*1;Leather*1
prop eeltrap loot.refill=0
note reedbox Reedcut box | A box in Reedcut: reed rope and a basket of eggs.
loot reedbox Rope*3;Egg*3
prop reedbox loot.refill=0
note eelbox Eelmarsh box | A box in Eelmarsh: smoked eel and line.
loot eelbox Cooked_Herring*3;FishingBait_Simple*2
prop eelbox loot.refill=0
note turfbox Turfholm box | A box in Turfholm: ore from a turf spade's iron, dry peat for a fire and a few planks.
loot turfbox MetalOre*2;BioFuel*1;Plank*3
prop turfbox loot.refill=0
note willowbox Willowbend box | A box in Willowbend: willow withies, a few planks and potatoes from the miller's sack.
loot willowbox Plank*4;Raw_Potato*3;Rope*2
prop willowbox loot.refill=0
note sunkpunt1 Sunk punt | A punt sunk in a channel with its load: crates of scrap.
loot sunkpunt1 Scrap*3;MetalOre*2;Nail*6
prop sunkpunt1 loot.refill=0
note sunkpunt2 Sunk punt | Another punt the fen swallowed: clay and copper.
loot sunkpunt2 Clay*3;CopperOre*2;Scrap*2
prop sunkpunt2 loot.refill=0

